# Pattern: Graceful Degradation

Purpose:
  Define degradation modes for the SDDRA system when components
  fail or resources are limited. Ensures system remains partially
  operational rather than completely failing.

## Degradation Modes

FULL:
  Description: All features operational
  Requirements: All components healthy
  Capabilities:
    - Full chain execution
    - All skills available
    - Full context loading
    - Human gates active

REDUCED:
  Description: Non-critical features disabled
  Trigger: Minor component failure, resource pressure
  Capabilities:
    - Chain execution (skip optional stages)
    - Core skills only
    - Reduced context (lazy loading)
    - Human gates active for critical items
  Restrictions:
    - Skip observability stages
    - Skip optional testing stages
    - Use cached contexts only

MINIMAL:
  Description: Essential features only
  Trigger: Major component failure, resource exhaustion
  Capabilities:
    - Basic chain execution (P1->D1->S1->C1 only)
    - Essential skills only
    - Minimal context
    - Human approval for all gates
  Restrictions:
    - No R1 (review) - human reviews manually
    - No DEP1 (deploy) - human deploys manually
    - No parallel execution
    - No caching

READ_ONLY:
  Description: Analysis only, no modifications
  Trigger: System instability, audit mode
  Capabilities:
    - Read .sdd/ files
    - Analyze project structure
    - Generate reports
  Restrictions:
    - No file creation
    - No modifications
    - No chain execution
    - No state changes

## Degradation Triggers

Resource-Based:
  - Memory > 90%: REDUCED
  - Memory > 95%: MINIMAL
  - Disk < 1GB: READ_ONLY
  - Token budget < 10%: MINIMAL

Component-Based:
  - Skill registry unavailable: REDUCED
  - Context cache corrupted: REDUCED
  - Graph engine failed: MINIMAL
  - State tracker failed: READ_ONLY

Failure-Based:
  - 1-2 stage failures: REDUCED
  - 3+ stage failures: MINIMAL
  - Critical component failure: READ_ONLY

## Degradation Actions

On Degradation:
  1. Detect degradation condition
  2. Determine appropriate mode
  3. Disable non-essential features
  4. Notify human of degraded state
  5. Continue with reduced capabilities
  6. Log degradation event

On Recovery:
  1. Detect component recovery
  2. Verify component health
  3. Restore previous mode
  4. Notify human of recovery
  5. Resume full capabilities

## Fallback Strategies

Stage Fallbacks:
  P1: Use cached analysis or ask human
  D1: Use template defaults or cached docs
  S1: Use template or cached .sdd/ state
  C1: Generate minimal code, human completes
  R1: Skip automated review, human reviews
  DEP1: Skip automated deploy, human deploys

Skill Fallbacks:
  - If specific skill missing: use generic skill
  - If skill fails: use manual process
  - If skill unavailable: skip stage

Context Fallbacks:
  - If context cache corrupted: rebuild from scratch
  - If context too large: reduce to essential only
  - If context missing: use defaults

## Monitoring

Metrics:
  current_mode: FULL|REDUCED|MINIMAL|READ_ONLY
  degradation_count: integer
  recovery_count: integer
  time_in_degraded: duration
  skipped_stages: list

Alerts:
  Mode change: notify human
  Extended degradation: escalate
  Recovery: log and notify

State: +
